  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "In many languages the same word covers **to**, **at**, and **in**; English separates movement (**to** the store) from position (**at** the store).",
    "grammar": "**Explain**, **say**, and **describe** need **to** before the person. In **look forward to** and **be used to**, **to** is a preposition and takes a noun or an **-ing** form, not the base form of a verb.",
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": null,
    "pronunciation": "**To** is usually said weakly, like *tuh*; learners who always say the full form, like **too**, sound too careful and can be hard to follow."
  },
